## 2. Core AAA Principles & Enhanced Rules

### Perceivable (Enhanced)
- **1.4.6 Contrast (Enhanced)**:
  - Normal text: Minimum **7:1** contrast ratio against background.
  - Large text (≥ 18pt / 24px or ≥ 14pt / 18.66px bold): Minimum **4.5:1** contrast ratio.
- **1.4.8 Visual Presentation**:
  - Maximum line width: **80 characters** (40 glyphs for CJK). Example: `max-width: 75ch;`.
  - Line height: At least **1.5** within paragraphs (`line-height: 1.6;`).
  - Paragraph spacing: At least **2.25 times font size** (e.g., `margin-top: 2.25em;`).
  - Text alignment: **NEVER use `text-align: justify`**. Only left-align (or right-align for RTL).
  - User theme controls: Provide user-selectable light/dark/high-contrast modes.
- **1.4.9 Images of Text (No Exception)**:
  - Do NOT use raster images of text (PNG/JPEG) except for logos. Use semantic typography, Web fonts, or accessible SVG.

### Operable (Enhanced)
- **2.1.3 Keyboard (No Exception)**:
  - Every single interaction, feature, and custom widget must be keyboard operable with **zero exceptions** (including drawing canvas or interactive maps with equivalent input controls).
- **2.2 Timing Controls**:
  - **2.2.3 No Timing**: No time limits, or allow disabling all timers.
  - **2.2.5 Re-authenticating**: If a session expires, allow re-authenticating without losing entered form data.
  - **2.2.6 Timeouts**: Warn users at start of activity about any inactivity timeout.
- **2.3 Animations & Flashing**:
  - **2.3.2 Three Flashes**: Zero content flashes more than 3 times per second.
  - **2.3.3 Animation from Interactions**: Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and allow disabling non-essential user-triggered motion.
- **2.5.5 Target Size (Enhanced)**:
  - Interactive touch/pointer targets must be at least **44×44 CSS pixels** (`min-width: 44px; min-height: 44px;`).

### Understandable (Enhanced)
- **3.1.3 & 3.1.4 Unusual Words & Abbreviations**:
  - Provide definition tooltips or links using `<dfn>` for technical jargon or idioms.
  - Provide expansions for abbreviations using `<abbr title="expanded form">` or expand on first use.
- **3.1.5 Reading Level**:
  - Provide clear, simple summaries when text exceeds lower secondary education reading level.
- **3.2.5 Change on Request**:
  - Changes of context must occur ONLY on explicit user request (e.g. clicking a submit/action button), never on input, select, or focus.
- **3.3.5 Error Prevention (All)**:
  - All form submissions (not just financial/legal) MUST provide either:
    1. Reversible submissions, OR
    2. Real-time validation with opportunity to correct, OR
    3. A mandatory confirmation review step before final submission.
- **3.3.6 Context-Sensitive Help**:
  - Every form input must have persistent helper text or an accessible help popover.

---

## 3. Production Verification Protocol
1. Run axe-core with AAA rules: `npx @axe-core/cli <url> --tags wcag2aaa`.
2. Inspect color contrast against the strict **7:1** threshold.
3. Verify target sizes meet **44×44 CSS px**.
4. Test keyboard focus with sticky headers to confirm **100% visibility (zero obscurity)**.
5. Verify focus indicator satisfies the **2.4.13 appearance formula** (≥2px perimeter & ≥3:1 contrast).
